@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Rolling-Restart System-Theory Snapshot
+
+This is a historical worked example, not steering or current Quest truth. Verify
+it against a current measured run before reusing any hypothesis.
+
+At the time of capture, repeated coupled-invariant oscillation between the
+`publication_converged` / `priority_spread_settled` family and dependent
+families suggested a shared admission/readiness knob. The `CoupledAdmission`
+model showed one overlapping green value, suggesting that isolated owner
+patches would bounce while an atomic cross-owner reconcile could converge.
+
+The claim remained unconfirmed because the relevant harness samples were not
+measuring. Its durable lesson is the method: turn coupled oscillation into a
+falsifiable system theory and confirm it with fresh measured evidence. The
+specific rolling-restart state belongs to its Quest log and reports.
